Install and update (macOS)
--------------------------
Open the .dmg and drag Burnout3Takedown.app to Applications, replacing the
old one for an update. The game files are inside the app. To uninstall,
drag the app to the Trash; your saves stay in Application Support.

The app is signed ad hoc on the Mac that built it, not notarized. On
another Mac, Gatekeeper may refuse it: right-click > Open once, or run
  xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Burnout3Takedown.app

To keep saves and settings somewhere else, set BURNOUT3TAKEDOWN_DATA_DIR
to that folder before starting the game.

Options
-------
Your options live in config/config.toml in
~/Library/Application Support/Burnout3Takedown. The app's
Contents/Resources/config.default.toml lists every option at its stock
value. Copy a line from it into your config.toml and change it there, for
example "scale = 2" under "[render]" to draw at twice the resolution. An
update replaces config.default.toml but never touches your file.

Controls
--------
Use a controller (Xbox, PlayStation or another SDL-supported pad); it is
player 1, and a second one is player 2 (the split-screen modes). The
keyboard works too, as player 1, while the game window has the focus
(RECOMP_KEYBOARD=0 in config/launch.env turns it off):

  arrows          d-pad            Enter       START
  Z X C V         A B X Y          Backspace   BACK
  Q E             white, black     1 3         left, right trigger
  W/S/A/D         left stick       I/K/J/L     right stick
  numpad 8/2/4/6  left stick too   Shift Ctrl  left, right stick click

Speed
-----
The game steps a fixed amount per frame. On a machine that cannot keep up,
races play in slow motion but correctly.

Known gaps on the Mac
---------------------
The title screen and menu music is silent (the intro movies and the races
have sound).
